---
title: A Very Simple Rajma
source: https://cygopi.wordpress.com/2007/02/18/a-very-simple-rajma
servings: 5
---

Boil @rajma{500%g} for ~{30%minutes} or ~{40%minutes} until it is tender. If using a #pressure cooker{}, that’s six or seven whistles.

In two tablespoons of @oil{} or @ghee{}, fry @onion{150%g}(sliced into rings) until golden brown. Add @tomato{150%g}(chopped coarsely), stir a bit, then add @red chilly powder{1%tsp} and @salt{} to taste. Stir some more.

Now grind this mixture to a fine paste. Pour this over the boiled rajma, add hot water until you have a medium thin gravy, and simmer, covered, for another ~{30%minutes} or allow six to seven whistles more on the pressure cooker. 

That’s it. Do not mash. Do not garnish with coriander. Do not garnish with anything. Do not add garam masala. Do not speak while eating.